<article class="env-definition" id="08AD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08AD">Definition <span data-tag="08AD">33.35.15</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $n \geq 0$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent sheaf on $\mathbf{P}^ n_ k$. The function $d \mapsto \chi (\mathbf{P}^ n_ k, \mathcal{F}(d))$ is called the <em>Hilbert polynomial</em> of $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
